#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:5
#: 8822fb5f01ab421b8e0f288ae6989cc7
msgid "ZigZag Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:7
#: 776601ee741547d3aebb5af80b7a17d0
msgid "ZigZag mode is a semi-autonomous mode designed to make it easier for a pilot to fly a vehicle back and forth across a field which can be useful for crop spraying"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:12
#: 06f00147cbfe4f50b27d4cd2465c39eb
msgid "The way it works is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:14
#: 7b35a41960394388be556b24f29672b3
msgid "A two or three position :ref:`auxiliary switch <channel-7-and-8-options>` is set to 61 / \"ZigZag SaveWP\" (i.e. :ref:`RC7_OPTION <RC7_OPTION>` = 61)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:15
#: 1c19383a77ee479ab2d295406189f1bd
msgid "The pilot arms the vehicle and takes off.  The vehicle will fly just like :ref:`Loiter <loiter-mode>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:16
#: 1c92d79e0612404e8c31cafeecf742b6
msgid "The vehicle is flown manually to one side of the field and then the auxiliary switch is moved to the highest or lowest position (it doesn't matter which) to record that side"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:17
#: bbadc37b992c4076b2bd88d1aace768b
msgid "The vehicle is flown to the other side of the field and the switch is moved to the opposite position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:18
#: ac823b9cd6964b7c8cd935e15e8877ea
msgid "The switch can now be used to start the vehicle flying autonomously (at the current height) to either side of the field.  Once the vehicle reaches the other side it will revert to manual control.  The pilot can also regain manual control by moving the auxiliary switch to the middle position or by changing the flight mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:19
#: b64c9a01e7254be3bb3770fc19efd255
msgid "If a downward facing :ref:`range finder <common-rangefinder-landingpage>` is used, the vehicle will follow the terrain when flying.  If the range finder becomes unhealthy while traversing from one side to the other, the vehicle will revert to manual control and come to a stop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:25
#: b3cdc23f414246108536072b770397a0
msgid "When flown manually ZigZag uses :ref:`Loiter mode's <loiter-mode>`  parameters.  For example the top speed can be configured with :ref:`LOIT_SPEED_MS<LOIT_SPEED_MS>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:27
#: f56006ad192c404c9dd7401eb21e2797
msgid "When autonomously flying from one side of the field to the other, the :ref:`Auto mode <auto-mode>` parameters are used.  For example the top speed can be configured with :ref:`WP_SPD<WP_SPD>`.."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:32
#: 2ad5a7d19d684043960e891ee8aebbf6
msgid "Automatic Operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:34
#: f16e083246fb4660a53e387ebfd878f9
msgid "This feature will be available in Copter-4.1.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:36
#: ed18776e89bf4a5a9aa9b275456477ae
msgid "this function must be enabled with :ref:`ZIGZ_AUTO_ENABLE<ZIGZ_AUTO_ENABLE>` = 1, and parameters reloaded, before any parameters are visible and the feature enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:38
#: ea5a906a7d914b0b9ffa0da6abb447ea
msgid "After the field's side points are registered, if you have an RC switch configured with ``RCx_OPTION`` = 83 (ZigZag Auto Mode), you can automatically cover the field side to side at a programmable distance interval, also enabling a sprayer, if equipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:43
#: 28452a5f540d4f10bd16a5e0914ff0b6
msgid "To use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:45
#: a7d0dc18f1df4cf896070c4da2f81903
msgid "Fly to one side of the field and register the ZigZagWP A, as above, then fly to ZigZagWP B and set it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:46
#: 9a34a3e7258740c78d1c091990b57d22
msgid "Then switch the ZigZag Auto Mode switch you had setup. The vehicle will proceed as shown in the diagram, automatically enabling a sprayer, if setup. See :ref:`sprayer` for instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:47
#: 47cc7cba9dd44250a05f5b6b50435124
msgid "Upon activation, the vehicle will move in :ref:`ZIGZ_DIRECTION<ZIGZ_DIRECTION>` with respect to its heading for :ref:`ZIGZ_SIDE_DIST<ZIGZ_SIDE_DIST>`, then proceed to cross the field until the opposite ZigZagWP is reached. It will then wait for :ref:`ZIGZ_WP_DELAY<ZIGZ_WP_DELAY>` to allow sprayer to fully stop and then move :ref:`ZIGZ_SIDE_DIST<ZIGZ_SIDE_DIST>` down the side of the field again to proceed back across the area. It will do this for :ref:`ZIGZ_LINE_NUM<ZIGZ_LINE_NUM>` times (-1 = infinite until switched out of this mode, =0 will only move to the first field crossing position, but not proceed further)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:49
#: b48c060a03ee4113a232ba767961291f
msgid "Moving the ZigZag Auto switch to the low position immediately stops this mode and returns to normal ZIGZAG mode."
msgstr ""
